1
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,197
-t-t-t-t

2
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:13,280
-t

3
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:19,680
It's enough crying.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,529
And enough sitting around.

5
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:26,480
It's time to make a decision.

6
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:29,097
I've got to go.

7
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:31,360
They're all fighting for me.

8
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:33,090
Please.

9
00:00:33,173 --> 00:00:34,140
Breathe.

10
00:00:39,440 --> 00:00:41,237
You need to come back now!

11
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:42,437
Before it's too late!

12
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:44,280
For your friends.

13
00:00:50,720 --> 00:00:52,897
I must have been dreaming.

14
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:54,817
For a moment there?

15
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:56,959
I thought we actually had a chance.

16
00:00:58,020 --> 00:01:01,780
Uh, so what did that shark
guy just do? I don't know.

17
00:01:02,180 --> 00:01:05,062
It looked like he was just
throwing water around.

18
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,820
But then they both started to bleed.

19
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:10,700
I don't even have to touch you.

20
00:01:11,080 --> 00:01:13,937
You humans are so fragile
that I can kill you

21
00:01:14,020 --> 00:01:16,549
just by playing around
with a little water.

22
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:19,392
That's the difference between you and me.

23
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:20,440
Shut up!

24
00:01:27,340 --> 00:01:28,500
He's not kidding.

25
00:01:37,120 --> 00:01:39,860
That's why the shark
is king of the fishmen.

26
00:01:43,120 --> 00:01:45,220
He's on a whole different level.

27
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:47,060
You should just die.

28
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,960
Your lives are not worth that much.

29
00:01:50,340 --> 00:01:52,617
There's no one who will
miss you when you're gone.

30
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:53,530
Arlong!

31
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:55,640
It's Nami.

32
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:56,960
You're here.

33
00:01:58,460 --> 00:01:59,720
Hey, Nami.

34
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:04,480
I was just teaching one final lesson
to these pathetic little pirates.

35
00:02:05,080 --> 00:02:07,040
What are you doing here?

36
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:14,200
I'm here to kill you.

37
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,700
Wealth, fame, power.

38
00:02:18,020 --> 00:02:19,637
Gold Roger, the king of the pirates,

39
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,097
attained this and everything
else the world had to offer.

40
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:25,400
and his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

41
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:27,015
You want my treasure?

42
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,480
You can have it.

43
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:31,660
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

44
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:34,100
Now you just have to find it.

45
00:02:35,940 --> 00:02:39,277
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuit

46
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:41,817
of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine.

47
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:44,665
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

48
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:49,917
Come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

49
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:55,440
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

50
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,740
One piece.

51
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:07,577
Compass left behind,
he'll only slow us down.

52
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:13,457
Your heart will be your guide,
raise the sails and take the helm.

53
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:19,177
That legendary place that
the end of the map reveals.

54
00:03:19,260 --> 00:03:25,237
It's only legendary until
someone proves it real.

55
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:29,497
Through it all, through
all the trouble of times.

56
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:31,857
Through the heartache
and through the pain.

57
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:36,220
Know that I will be there to stand by you.

58
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:39,300
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

59
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:45,457
So come aboard and bring along
all your hopes and dreams.

60
00:03:45,540 --> 00:03:51,040
Together we will find everything
that we're looking for.

61
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:54,677
There's always room for you.

62
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:57,377
If you wanna be my friend.

63
00:03:57,460 --> 00:04:01,920
We are, we are on a cruise.

64
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:04,740
We are

65
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:07,800
Me?

66
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:11,080
You want to kill me?

67
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:20,057
hasn't you learned your lesson
yet how many times have you tried

68
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:25,780
to kill me in these last eight
years um you've tried Assassination

69
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:27,470
um

70
00:04:30,460 --> 00:04:34,520
you must be aware that you
mere humans can't kill me

71
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:42,460
Now listen, I won't put you in the
ground, Nami But you can't leave

72
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:50,740
You will remain here, with
us, as our surveyor, forever

73
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:53,580
But as you know,

74
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:56,557
I'm quite good-natured If possible,

75
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:59,758
I'd like you to be our
surveyor of your own free will

76
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:07,020
I'm giving you a choice.

77
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:11,057
I will not take pause in having my fishmen

78
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:13,437
kill every living creature on this island.

79
00:05:13,520 --> 00:05:14,660
Except for you.

80
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:19,657
But that's only if you
refuse to come back to the

81
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:22,858
Arlong Pirates and draw sea
sharks as one of our own.

82
00:05:25,240 --> 00:05:27,357
And if you decide to come back with us,

83
00:05:27,440 --> 00:05:30,322
I'll be kind and spare
the villagers their lives.

84
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:34,217
But I can't let these ingrates live.

85
00:05:34,300 --> 00:05:37,417
They must be made an example of.

86
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,400
So there's only one question!

87
00:05:40,860 --> 00:05:44,720
Will you come with me and save
the people of Cocoyashi village?

88
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:49,997
Or be foolish and refuse my
request by fighting alongside them?

89
00:05:50,080 --> 00:05:51,820
It's your choice!

90
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:54,157
With them you will be hopeless.

91
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:56,520
With them you will die.

92
00:06:03,420 --> 00:06:04,250
Nami.

93
00:06:04,333 --> 00:06:06,420
Will you come and stand by my side?

94
00:06:06,800 --> 00:06:07,697
Or not?

95
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:10,200
The decision is yours.

96
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:15,560
This isn't fair.

97
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:20,156
If I remain friends with Luffy and
the others, everyone will be killed.

98
00:06:20,280 --> 00:06:23,397
But if I go with Arlong, everyone
from the village will be saved.

99
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,900
Their lives depend on my choice.

100
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:30,280
Not fair!

101
00:06:30,580 --> 00:06:33,698
No matter what she chooses,
he'll never set her free!

102
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:36,650
But...

103
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:42,730
Luffy...

104
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:45,577
Help me...

105
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:47,040
That's for Nami!

106
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:53,740
I have to believe in him!

107
00:06:58,340 --> 00:07:02,600
All right, everyone, we'll
fight to the death, got it?

108
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:17,920
Well then, it looks like
they've made up their minds.

109
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:28,280
Please, Liv! Please, Liv!

110
00:07:47,080 --> 00:07:49,820
Alright, now just remove his leg weight.

111
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:51,340
I see.

112
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:55,140
That's what you meant.

113
00:07:55,460 --> 00:07:56,400
No way!

114
00:07:57,080 --> 00:07:58,300
Luffy's alive!

115
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:01,400
Hey! Hang in there!

116
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:03,100
You can't give up now!

117
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,560
Thirty seconds.

118
00:08:17,540 --> 00:08:18,840
That's all I've got.

119
00:08:21,340 --> 00:08:22,170
Zoro!

120
00:08:23,740 --> 00:08:24,799
That'll be enough!

121
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:28,600
There isn't a fountain over there.

122
00:08:29,060 --> 00:08:30,740
Could it be that rubber man?

123
00:08:36,940 --> 00:08:38,120
Just stay back.

124
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,680
You're not getting anywhere near him.

125
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:42,670
Ah, Zoro.

126
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:45,600
I thought I told you to
never say that again.

127
00:08:46,060 --> 00:08:47,780
Now prepare to die!

128
00:08:53,740 --> 00:08:56,940
If I kick and break that
leg weight, he can fight.

129
00:08:57,540 --> 00:09:00,560
Luffy, you're the only
one who can fight now.

130
00:09:05,660 --> 00:09:06,657
In the sea,

131
00:09:06,740 --> 00:09:11,211
one with Devil Fruit powers is supposed
to lose even the energy to struggle.

132
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:13,260
Not to mention his powers.

133
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:15,140
He will die.

134
00:09:16,460 --> 00:09:19,860
And if he's still alive,
well, that wouldn't be fair.

135
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:22,090
You okay?

136
00:09:22,173 --> 00:09:25,957
hey Lisa you're fine sure I'm fine

137
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:29,337
you scared us where'd your pinwheel

138
00:09:29,420 --> 00:09:35,217
go it was cool we've got bigger things
to worry about right now wouldn't

139
00:09:35,300 --> 00:09:39,777
be fair this game hasn't been fair
from the moment we started playing

140
00:09:39,860 --> 00:09:46,260
it well anyways if there's a hindrance
I should be aware of it correct

141
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:54,060
I've got your back, Zoro!

142
00:09:54,860 --> 00:09:57,260
Big bro Usopp, he's all right!

143
00:09:57,520 --> 00:09:58,400
How brave!

144
00:09:58,760 --> 00:10:00,820
And he got here just in time.

145
00:10:01,520 --> 00:10:02,940
Go on, give it to him!

146
00:10:03,740 --> 00:10:04,975
That's where you are?

147
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:07,040
He's all right!

148
00:10:07,700 --> 00:10:08,700
Hey, hey, Nami!

149
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:11,157
I beat one of their
leaders, can you believe it?

150
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:13,416
I wiped the smug off his stupid face!

151
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:16,777
Think, is there any way
you can free yourself?

152
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:18,260
Nope, can't do it.

153
00:10:18,540 --> 00:10:20,069
The energy is way too low.

154
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:23,180
C'mon! C'mon! C'mon! C'mon!

155
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:28,440
All right, cook!

156
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:32,080
Now, if they can just
set Big Bro Luffy free,

157
00:10:32,360 --> 00:10:36,120
the fishmen will be running
for their lives! Go, Zoro!

158
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:39,240
Take down Arlong once and for all!

159
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:46,102
Okay, we have to somehow prevent
Arlong from getting into the sea.

160
00:10:46,780 --> 00:10:49,074
I'll just keep him from going anywhere.

161
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:56,820
I won't let you have your way.

162
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:59,740
Hey, Harlong, I've got a present for you!

163
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,440
What's he doing?

164
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:05,440
He's so brave!

165
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:12,200
You seem to keep standing in my way.

166
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:14,777
I take it you wish to die first, then.

167
00:11:14,860 --> 00:11:16,272
I can take care of that.

168
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:17,840
Zoro, now!

169
00:11:18,460 --> 00:11:20,695
What do you think you're doing, Usopp?

170
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:24,520
Now's my chance.

171
00:11:24,740 --> 00:11:26,622
All I want is a piece of that...

172
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:32,900
You fool.

173
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:36,360
It's a proud nose
because it's unbreakable.

174
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:40,000
If you were in full strength,

175
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:44,200
you may have been able to
give it a little scratch.

176
00:12:00,540 --> 00:12:06,500
Look over there that damn octopus is up

177
00:12:18,480 --> 00:12:19,310
What?!

178
00:12:20,420 --> 00:12:21,250
What?!

179
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:25,025
He's the one I was aiming for!

180
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:28,720
But weren't you yelling Arlong, huh?

181
00:12:29,600 --> 00:12:30,560
Oh, great.

182
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:32,820
We're not done, Zoro!

183
00:12:33,200 --> 00:12:35,897
You may have put me down,
but it wasn't for good!

184
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:39,686
Cause I'm still alive and now
I'm gonna finish off your friend!

185
00:12:47,280 --> 00:12:51,680
No need to be concerned seeing as
how you will all be dead anyway

186
00:13:10,040 --> 00:13:11,800
You've done enough, Nojiko.

187
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:13,420
Leave the rest to me!

188
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,600
Watch out!

189
00:13:21,820 --> 00:13:23,702
I'll break the rock with a kick!

190
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:30,830
What?

191
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:33,360
Octopus-Fla-Renzy!

192
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:35,630
No!

193
00:13:42,080 --> 00:13:42,910
Thoreau!

194
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:49,200
So, that's it, huh?

195
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:50,600
Way too easy.

196
00:13:52,900 --> 00:13:55,000
What's with all these bandages?

197
00:13:56,880 --> 00:13:58,800
Did you have a good fall?

198
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:05,420
What's this scar?

199
00:14:19,920 --> 00:14:26,160
I can't believe he's breathing how can
he still be alive with a body like this

200
00:14:38,020 --> 00:14:39,780
Is he dying already?

201
00:14:40,820 --> 00:14:42,900
Am I fighting a wounded man?

202
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:47,600
Either way, he's about to die.

203
00:14:49,220 --> 00:14:51,680
He's going to die right here and now.

204
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:03,500
If a person stays put,
their wounds won't open up.

205
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:07,337
Is that right?

206
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:10,240
Do you find your situation amusing?

207
00:15:14,100 --> 00:15:16,017
I'm not talking about me.

208
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:18,380
I'm talking about the Octoman.

209
00:15:19,620 --> 00:15:20,450
What?

210
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:23,757
I thought we told you.

211
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:25,680
We'll win this game.

212
00:15:35,420 --> 00:15:36,940
That was too close.

213
00:15:43,880 --> 00:15:47,468
You're the one that made this
complicated in the first place.

214
00:15:50,060 --> 00:15:51,280
He did it!

215
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:53,796
It's time to take care of that shark.

216
00:15:54,420 --> 00:15:55,740
Hurry up, you idiot!

217
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:01,160
Did they free you? Yes!

218
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:18,640
It's him!

219
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:21,260
A hero back!

220
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,520
Luffy!

221
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:34,980
That rubber bastard!

222
00:16:36,520 --> 00:16:38,600
You're a bit late.

223
00:16:42,520 --> 00:16:44,720
Hey, hold on.

224
00:16:45,220 --> 00:16:46,520
What are you...

225
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:51,940
Let's switch!

226
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:56,060
You idiot!

227
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:58,760
Come go!

228
00:17:02,140 --> 00:17:04,300
Oh, no! Oh, that way!

229
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:13,420
Oh, no!

230
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:15,230
Take care!

231
00:17:19,540 --> 00:17:20,900
Help me!

232
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:32,220
Yes!

233
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:51,060
Is that all you got?

234
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:53,800
It's not working!

235
00:17:54,940 --> 00:17:57,020
Nope, just a warm one.

236
00:18:00,480 --> 00:18:01,310
Ugh.

237
00:18:01,393 --> 00:18:02,237
That idiot.

238
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:03,760
I'm gonna kill him.

239
00:18:07,520 --> 00:18:09,257
What a bunch of fools.

240
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:11,500
You think you can actually beat me?

241
00:18:11,720 --> 00:18:14,780
You were better off
drowning on the ocean floor.

242
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:17,020
No, I don't think so.

243
00:18:17,440 --> 00:18:18,940
I like it up here. Yep.

244
00:18:23,420 --> 00:18:25,900
Do you not understand my anger?

245
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:29,500
I saw my brothers crushed like worms.

246
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:35,680
You'll realize soon enough that you
should have quit fighting a long time ago.

247
00:18:36,840 --> 00:18:39,100
Do you think Luffy's gonna be okay?

248
00:18:39,520 --> 00:18:43,344
I mean, Arlong doesn't seem to be
affected by his attacks at all.

249
00:18:43,460 --> 00:18:47,166
And more importantly, just how
far away do you think Zoro flew?

250
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:48,537
Luffy!

251
00:18:48,620 --> 00:18:50,280
I got your back, pal!

252
00:18:50,740 --> 00:18:52,080
No need to worry.

253
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:02,980
If he loses, then we'll all die.

254
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:05,580
Yeah, we will.

255
00:19:05,860 --> 00:19:09,240
If that happens, it's the
end of the East Blue, too.

256
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:21,000
Do you know what the biggest difference
between you and me is the nose?

257
00:19:23,820 --> 00:19:24,960
The jaw.

258
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:30,597
Um what's he doing uh

259
00:19:30,680 --> 00:19:34,460
i don't know webbing.

260
00:19:36,800 --> 00:19:37,630
Species!

261
00:19:50,660 --> 00:19:51,490
Oh, man!

262
00:19:51,680 --> 00:19:53,386
I bet that had to be painful!

263
00:19:53,560 --> 00:19:55,207
His teeth must be shattered!

264
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:23,217
You see this is the
inherent power of this man.

265
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:28,297
I feel sorry for you, pathetic humans,
having been created with such limited power.

266
00:20:28,380 --> 00:20:32,657
We've been on a different level than
you since the beginning of time.

267
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:37,387
Being such inferior creatures, it makes
perfect sense for you to bow before me.

268
00:20:46,080 --> 00:20:46,910
He's right.

269
00:20:46,993 --> 00:20:49,257
There's no way a human could
do something like that.

270
00:20:49,340 --> 00:20:51,177
If those jaws got a hold of you,

271
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:55,180
they would do a lot more than
just leave some bite marks.

272
00:21:00,720 --> 00:21:03,367
He'll snap through your
bones like a butcher.

273
00:21:07,020 --> 00:21:08,560
Yeah, so what?

274
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:11,500
Quit your bragging.

275
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:14,020
You're not that awesome.

276
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:21,632
Besides, smashing stones with
your teeth isn't that smart.

277
00:21:24,560 --> 00:21:26,997
Way to go, you're the best, big bro.

278
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:28,537
Tell it like it is. Yeah.

279
00:21:28,620 --> 00:21:30,444
What idiot bites a rock anyway?

280
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:33,630
Fools.

281
00:21:33,713 --> 00:21:34,637
That's not the point.

282
00:21:34,720 --> 00:21:38,577
Every member of the human
race is ignorant and weak.

283
00:21:38,660 --> 00:21:42,601
What good are you if you can't even
pull yourself out of the water?

284
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:50,859
As a matter of fact, I'm worthless
without my friends to help me out.

285
00:21:56,180 --> 00:21:57,560
Huh? No way!

286
00:21:57,760 --> 00:21:58,936
Luffy's a swordsman?

287
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:03,830
Huh?

288
00:22:03,913 --> 00:22:04,743
Is this a joke?

289
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:06,939
Whatever it is, it isn't swordplay.

290
00:22:07,200 --> 00:22:10,494
You're just flailing about
like a child playing pirates.

291
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:20,880
I hope you realize this isn't a game.

292
00:22:30,300 --> 00:22:32,340
That's enough! Now die!

293
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:35,040
Shut your face!

294
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:56,990
What?!

295
00:22:57,073 --> 00:22:58,840
He just shattered our mom's tea!

296
00:23:02,740 --> 00:23:03,570
You're right!

297
00:23:03,653 --> 00:23:06,699
I don't have a clue how to
use a sword, you bastard!

298
00:23:06,980 --> 00:23:09,900
Wait, what exactly is
he trying to say here?

299
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:15,200
I'm a terrible sailor.

300
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:18,780
I definitely can't cook.

301
00:23:20,180 --> 00:23:22,740
And I can't even lie! Hey!

302
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:27,893
And without my friends to help me, I
would have been dead a long time ago!

303
00:23:30,440 --> 00:23:33,197
So you fully admit how pathetic you are.

304
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:36,900
You may be a fool, but
you certainly are honest.

305
00:23:37,300 --> 00:23:41,900
How must your crew feel tolerating
this idiocy day in and day out?

306
00:23:42,140 --> 00:23:43,720
I bet they're sick of it.

307
00:23:45,020 --> 00:23:47,837
But that makes me wonder why they tried so

308
00:23:47,920 --> 00:23:50,391
desperately to save their half-wit leader.

309
00:23:51,620 --> 00:23:54,561
Someone like you doesn't
deserve a ship or a crew.

310
00:23:54,900 --> 00:23:57,937
What good is a helpless
rubber-brained captain to them?

311
00:23:58,020 --> 00:23:59,660
What can you possibly do?

312
00:24:00,820 --> 00:24:02,580
I can kick your ass!

313
00:24:05,720 --> 00:24:08,100
Well, get to it, you numbskull.

314
00:24:08,320 --> 00:24:10,640
If he dies, I'm going to kill him.

315
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:13,409
I've got your back, Luffy.

316
00:24:14,340 --> 00:24:16,080
All right, Kong!

317
00:24:16,520 --> 00:24:17,360
Let it be!

318
00:24:18,460 --> 00:24:20,260
Yeah, go for it!

319
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:24,824
Cheer all you want, but
it won't change a thing.

320
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:28,040
He's got no teeth.

321
00:24:28,560 --> 00:24:29,620
I'm a shark.

322
00:24:30,280 --> 00:24:32,157
New teeth will grow one after another.

323
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:35,540
And with each set, they
become stronger and stronger.

324
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:39,710
Endlessly.

325
00:24:46,160 --> 00:24:47,860
As many as it takes.

326
00:24:55,320 --> 00:24:58,820
This is but one of the many
gifts we fistmen possess.

327
00:25:00,900 --> 00:25:01,820
That's so cool!

328
00:25:02,920 --> 00:25:08,000
If you haven't yet realized that these
men are superior, you will very soon.

329
00:25:12,940 --> 00:25:13,820
Tooth, attack!

330
00:25:30,060 --> 00:25:32,100
Let's roll of me!

331
00:25:41,780 --> 00:25:44,260
Our long leaps.

332
00:25:44,820 --> 00:25:46,360
It hurts.

333
00:25:46,900 --> 00:25:47,730
What?

334
00:25:47,813 --> 00:25:48,660
My brother!

335
00:25:51,800 --> 00:25:54,800
You're dead, you stretchy freak!

336
00:25:56,060 --> 00:25:59,417
How dare you use my injured
brother as a shield?

337
00:25:59,500 --> 00:26:01,457
What are you talking about?

338
00:26:01,540 --> 00:26:02,937
You're the one who attacked me!

339
00:26:03,020 --> 00:26:06,897
Don't you remember that was pretty scary?

340
00:26:06,980 --> 00:26:12,577
Don't move a muscle!

341
00:26:12,660 --> 00:26:14,460
Rubber man!

342
00:26:16,500 --> 00:26:17,330
Hey!

343
00:26:17,413 --> 00:26:18,997
Now that's an interesting idea!

344
00:26:19,080 --> 00:26:20,617
He's got an idea!

345
00:26:20,700 --> 00:26:22,657
It's in his brain!

346
00:26:22,740 --> 00:26:24,417
Did he come up with?

347
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:25,912
With some secret scheme?

348
00:26:51,320 --> 00:26:54,120
All right!

349
00:26:58,080 --> 00:26:58,910
You.

350
00:26:58,993 --> 00:26:59,823
You fool.

351
00:27:00,020 --> 00:27:02,255
There's no point in crushing my teeth.

352
00:27:03,360 --> 00:27:05,320
You really don't get it!

353
00:27:07,120 --> 00:27:10,760
Big Bro, Luffy, that
can't be very sanitary.

354
00:27:11,580 --> 00:27:12,410
So what?

355
00:27:12,493 --> 00:27:13,860
Now I have short teeth!

356
00:27:25,920 --> 00:27:28,720
How long do you intend
to keep fooling around?

357
00:27:33,160 --> 00:27:34,340
Don't beat me!

358
00:27:37,100 --> 00:27:38,760
So stop playing games!

359
00:27:40,460 --> 00:27:42,360
It's not like I'm having fun!

360
00:27:43,320 --> 00:27:44,150
Unattack!

361
00:28:08,100 --> 00:28:09,300
Oh, no!

362
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:18,310
Gotcha!

363
00:28:18,680 --> 00:28:20,060
And now we're even!

364
00:28:21,840 --> 00:28:23,680
So you used my tea.

365
00:28:26,860 --> 00:28:29,580
But your puny jaws aren't strong enough.

366
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:32,560
Now listen, sharp as my teeth are,

367
00:28:32,800 --> 00:28:35,577
they're only useful when they
come with powerful jaws like mine.

368
00:28:35,660 --> 00:28:37,080
Then they're DEADLY!

369
00:28:39,560 --> 00:28:40,390
Ah!

370
00:28:40,680 --> 00:28:42,974
Big Bro's gonna get his arm bitten off!

371
00:28:51,840 --> 00:28:56,317
All that's in my heart confuses
me, I cannot understand.

372
00:28:56,400 --> 00:29:01,357
As I face what I must do, I'll
say goodbye and squeeze your hand!

373
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:06,337
I'll set sail alone, but always
know I'm dying, I'll keep you near.

374
00:29:06,420 --> 00:29:11,040
As I drift away, I pray you
watch me as I disappear.

375
00:29:16,440 --> 00:29:21,077
As I watched the sunrise,
I began to wonder?

376
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:25,800
What could be the reason
it's so hot inside?

377
00:29:26,280 --> 00:29:31,857
No answer has come, but I can't
get away from what's true.

378
00:29:31,940 --> 00:29:34,600
It's because of you!

379
00:29:37,220 --> 00:29:42,017
Show me how to catch those feelings,
get them to come back to me?

380
00:29:42,100 --> 00:29:47,137
I'll do what I must because
they're everything I want of me.

381
00:29:47,220 --> 00:29:51,617
Wrap these arms around my dreams
and pull them back from yesterday.

382
00:29:51,700 --> 00:29:57,120
If I'm holding hands with you,
I'm sure that we can make a way!
